<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Later Zhou</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Later Zhou was the last of the Five Dynasties that ruled northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in the tenth century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song">Zhao Kuangyin</a>, one of its military commanders, seized power in a coup in 960 and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a>. The Later Zhou's reforms and army formed part of the base on which the Song built.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/later-zhou.jpg" alt="Later Zhou" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SS · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Later_Zhou.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
